HEADER    ETHANOL, WITH EVERY BOND STATED
REMARK    The one PDB fixture whose purpose is the *hydrogen count* rather than
REMARK    cells, residues or record framing. PDB names no count of its own, so
REMARK    a reader has to imply one from the bonds -- and every atom here
REMARK    appears in a CONECT record, which is what lets an oracle compare the
REMARK    answer at all (#293).
REMARK
REMARK    The two fixtures beside this one are deliberately *partly* connected,
REMARK    and cannot serve: RDKit infers the missing bonds from geometry where
REMARK    this crate does not, so a formula comparison there measures bond
REMARK    perception rather than hydrogen counting.
REMARK
REMARK    Ethanol because it is the smallest molecule where the counts differ
REMARK    per atom: 3, 2, 1 for the two carbons and the oxygen. C2H6O when the
REMARK    counts are implied, C2O when they are not, which is what #285 wrote.
REMARK    Real geometry rather than the zeros our own writer emits, matching
REMARK    the other fixtures and giving a reader something to check by eye.
HETATM    1  C1  LIG A   1       0.000   0.000   0.000  1.00 10.00           C
HETATM    2  C2  LIG A   1       1.512   0.000   0.000  1.00 11.50           C
HETATM    3  O1  LIG A   1       2.052   1.318   0.000  1.00 12.75           O
CONECT    1    2
CONECT    2    1    3
CONECT    3    2
END
